pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% CHECKED DELETION reaches the same fabrication, and turns it into the OPPOSITE wrong verdict.
% With `strengthening_to_core on` a `delc` subproof is a proof by contradiction and registers no
% proofgoals, so `proofgoal 1` fabricated one; closing it discharged the deletion obligation and
% core constraint 2 left the database for free. What remains, `x1 >= 1`, is satisfied by the
% logged solution -- and the formula `x1 AND ~x1` is UNSATISFIABLE.
f 2 ;
strengthening_to_core on;
delc 2 : : subproof
proofgoal 1
rup >= 1 ;
qed;
qed;
sol x1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
